WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.010
SPEAKER: Do you know what
happens when you say, OK Google?

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.160
TinyML or Tiny Machine Learning
is one of the fastest growing

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.870
fields of machine learning.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.780
It sits right at the
intersection of embedded systems,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.660
algorithms, and computing hardware.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.860
TinyML is all about on-device machine
leanring right at the endpoint

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.500
where the data resides,
and it is fundamentally

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.610
different than running machine learning
in big data centers or in the cloud.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.470
You already know and take for granted
some existing applications with TinyML.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.730
For instance, when you say, hey
Siri, OK Google, or hey Alexa,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.830
you're seeing TinyML in action.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.890
But those applications are
just the tip of the iceberg.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.550
TinyML has many different use cases
ranging from smart home appliances

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.920
to medical devices,
and it has applications

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.170
even in wildlife conservation.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.570
This exciting new professional
certificate program

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.940
is a Harvard collaboration
with innovative members

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.740
of Google's TensorFlow team.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.190
This certificate combines
computer science with engineering,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.680
and it features real-world
application case studies

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.110
that examine TinyML deployments.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.360
This program takes you
through the foundations

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.130
of TinyML to deploying machine
learning on your very own device.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.740
In the Foundations of
TinyML course, you'll

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.980
learn the basics of embedded
computing and discover the language

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.200
behind Tiny Machine Learning.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.920
In course 2, which focuses
on applications of TinyML,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.980
you'll get the opportunity
to see TinyML in practice

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.560
and learn the code behind some of
the most common applications today.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.460
Finally in Deploying TinyML, you'll
write the machine learning code

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.980
using Google's latest TensorFlow
Lite for microcontrollers

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.370
and program your very own smart device.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.050
We're just beginning to explore
the full capabilities of TinyML.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.460
Imagine what we could do if there were
smart, ideally biodegradable machine

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.500
learning sensors everywhere.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.840
Be at the forefront of
this emerging technology,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.010
and start learning TinyML today.

